      "requirement": "Elwin→MurrayMay3,1859forwardedcontextknownbyDarwinMay6via2459. Noexactreceiptinferred, noDarwinvoice and nofullDarwin→Elwinreplyreconstructed. Keep1992publicationmetadataseparatefrom1859composition. CandidateXMLhashmisprintalreadycorrectedadditivelyinprimarysupplement; useactualprimarypin.",
      "explicit_prior_primary_reading_reused": "Complete seven substantive paragraphs plus closing and postscript, header, excluded salutation, six footnotes, bibliography and full TEI read. Elwin to Murray, May3,1859 ALS6pp;1992 is publication metadata. Elwin read the partial manuscript Murray allowed and consulted Lyell; neither full finished Origin reading nor total opposition to Darwin science is shown. First objection omits evidential detail despite twenty years work, second dry style; P4 expressly acknowledges many facts are present. Lyell agreement conditional on Elwin description, not independent read endorsement. P5 pigeon-first publication and priority concern reported by Elwin, not a recovered Lyell letter; P6 forecasts favourable reception, not actual outcome. P7 explicit forwarding intention, intellectual modesty and hope for prompt pigeon volume; P9 admits Journal title uncertainty. Apparatus says Murray forwarded this, while2459P1–2 evaluates Elwin/Lyell suggestions and supplies missing separateDarwin→Elwinreply for forwarding. Therefore knowledge byMay6, not physical receiptMay3 or whole-paragraph agreement. NeithermissingDarwinreplynorMurraycovernote reconstructed."
